  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are a mixed package: S2 sets an 8% failure cap with a 12-month retest pathway, S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 24 months and retrofit to 6 years, and S5 sets a 10/100k recall trigger with regulator review above 8. S4 requires built-in suppression from 36 months, and S1 mandates reporting all overheating incidents within 5 business days, with 24 hours for fatalities/ongoing serious hazards. Both red lines are satisfied: per-model results go to purchasers and regulators but not the general public, and suppression/retrofit deadlines match the agreed minimums."
 },
